<BaseLayout title="Disclaimer" description="Important limits concerning renter-friendly projects, products, safety and tenancy rules.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="section-kicker">Important context</p><h1>Disclaimer.</h1><p>“Renter-friendly” does not mean risk-free, universally compatible, or automatically permitted.</p></div></section>
<section class="container content-section"><div class="prose">
<h2>General information</h2><p>Content is for general informational and educational purposes. It is not individual legal, construction or electrical advice, and is not a warranty of a product, price, project or outcome.</p>
<h2>Products and surfaces vary</h2><p>Adhesives, removable wallpaper, hooks, tapes, floor covers and peel-and-stick finishes may damage paint, plaster, varnish, grout or other surfaces. Ratings and compatibility depend on the exact model and the manufacturer's stated conditions. Follow current instructions, test discreetly where appropriate, and stop if the surface is loose, damp, damaged or unstable.</p>
<h2>Costs and reversibility scores</h2><p>Costs are illustrative estimates, not quotes. Prices, taxes, delivery and tool needs vary by country and date. The reversibility score (1–5) is a planning tool and not a guarantee. First-hand tests will be identified only when actually performed.</p>
<h2>Tenancy and safety</h2><p>Check your lease and jurisdiction before drilling, painting, changing fixtures or installing adhesives. US law varies by state and municipality. The UK tenancy page focuses on England. Do not block smoke alarms, sprinklers, vents or escape routes, and do not modify fixed wiring or plumbing yourself. For electrical, structural, fire-safety, damp, mould or other hazardous issues, consult an appropriately qualified professional.</p>
<h2>Commercial relationships</h2><p>Affiliate links, paid placements and advertising must be disclosed when active. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
